# Cursor AI Rules for DYOS Flutter Project

## Project Context
- Flutter/Dart mobile app for couples
- Uses Riverpod for state management
- Firebase for backend (Auth, Firestore, Storage)
- GoRouter for navigation
- Freezed for data models

## Code Style
- Use single quotes for strings
- Prefer const constructors where possible
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Follow Flutter/Dart conventions
- Maximum line length: 100 characters

## Architecture
- Feature-based folder structure
- Separate presentation, data, and domain layers
- Use Riverpod providers for state management
- Use Freezed for immutable data models
- Use GoRouter for navigation

## Best Practices
- Always handle async operations with proper error handling
- Use type-safe models (Freezed)
- Validate user input
- Handle loading and error states in UI
- Write tests for critical functionality (especially pairing)

## Naming Conventions
- Files: snake_case (e.g., `home_screen.dart`)
- Classes: PascalCase (e.g., `HomeScreen`)
- Variables/functions: camelCase (e.g., `getUserData`)
- Constants: lowerCamelCase with const (e.g., `const appSpacing`)

## When Writing Code
- Add comments for complex logic
- Use meaningful names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Handle edge cases
- Consider error states
- Write tests for new features
